WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.150
Why does this chapter matter so much?

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.188
Because it's the first time
the program writes to a tenant.

3
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:09.318
The workbook's privileged-access
design gives it three things to build:

4
00:00:09.318 --> 00:00:11.068
the administrator policy set,

5
00:00:11.068 --> 00:00:15.828
the gate that demands a fresh phishing-resistant
proof from a compliant device at

6
00:00:15.828 --> 00:00:20.588
the moment someone elevates, and the custom
authentication strength both rely on.

7
00:00:20.588 --> 00:00:24.362
Unlike the first two chapters,
this code can change things.

8
00:00:24.362 --> 00:00:30.000
So its design is cautious on purpose: it
writes only when told, creates every new

9
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.620
policy in report-only, enforces only with
a separate switch, and never deletes.
